Converter::initialize(address _registry, address _wethAddress)
├── Given _registry is zero address
│   └── It should revert with RegistryClientZeroRegistry (from __RegistryClient_init)
├── Given _wethAddress is zero
│   └── It should revert with ConverterZeroAddress
├── Given valid parameters
│   ├── It should initialize UUPS / RegistryClient / Pausable / ReentrancyGuard
│   ├── It should set the WETH contract
│   ├── It should set the Registry
│   └── It should emit ConverterInitialized event
└── Given already initialized
    └── It should revert with InvalidInitialization

Converter::receive() external payable
├── Given ETH is sent to contract
│   ├── It should accept ETH
│   └── It should update contract balance (increase)
└── Given contract is paused
    └── It should still accept ETH (receive function has no restrictions)

Converter::wrapETH() payable
├── Given caller does not have caller permission (onlyCaller modifier)
│   └── It should revert with RegistryClientMissingRole(CONVERTER_CALLER_ROLE)
├── Given contract is paused
│   └── It should revert with EnforcedPause
├── Given amount is zero (msg.value == 0)
│   └── It should return early without wrapping (no-op)
└── Given amount is valid
    ├── It should call weth.deposit() with msg.value
    ├── It should safeTransfer WETH to caller
    └── It should emit ETHWrapped event

Converter::unwrapWETH(uint256 _amount, address _receiver)
├── Given caller does not have caller permission (onlyCaller modifier)
│   └── It should revert with RegistryClientMissingRole(CONVERTER_CALLER_ROLE)
├── Given contract is paused
│   └── It should revert with EnforcedPause
├── Given amount is zero
│   └── It should return early without unwrapping (no-op)
├── Given receiver is zero address
│   └── It should revert with ConverterZeroAddress
├── Given caller has insufficient WETH balance
│   └── It should revert with ERC20InsufficientBalance (from safeTransferFrom)
├── Given caller has insufficient WETH allowance for Converter
│   └── It should revert with ERC20InsufficientAllowance (from safeTransferFrom)
└── Given amount is valid and caller has sufficient WETH
    ├── It should transfer WETH from caller to Converter
    ├── It should call weth.withdraw() to unwrap
    ├── It should send native ETH to receiver
    └── It should emit WETHUnwrapped event

Converter::grantCallerRole(address _account)
├── Given caller is not the registered StrategyManager contract (onlyAuthContract)
│   └── It should revert with RegistryClientInvalidCaller
├── Given account is zero address
│   └── It should revert with ConverterZeroAddress
└── Given a StrategyManager caller and a valid account
    ├── It should delegate to Registry.grantRole(CONVERTER_CALLER_ROLE, account)
    ├── It should emit CallerRoleGranted event
    └── It should let the granted account call wrapETH / unwrapWETH / executeSwapExactAmountIn

Converter::revokeCallerRole(address _account)
├── Given caller is not the registered StrategyManager contract (onlyAuthContract)
│   └── It should revert with RegistryClientInvalidCaller
├── Given account is zero address
│   └── It should revert with ConverterZeroAddress
└── Given a StrategyManager caller and a valid account
    ├── It should delegate to Registry.revokeRole(CONVERTER_CALLER_ROLE, account)
    ├── It should emit CallerRoleRevoked event
    └── It should block the revoked account from wrapETH / unwrapWETH / executeSwapExactAmountIn

Converter::executeSwapExactAmountIn(address _adapter, bytes _path, uint256 _amountIn, uint256 _minAmountOut, uint256 _deadline)
├── Given caller does not have caller permission (onlyCaller modifier)
│   └── It should revert with RegistryClientMissingRole(CONVERTER_CALLER_ROLE)
├── Given contract is paused
│   └── It should revert with EnforcedPause
├── Given amountIn is zero
│   └── It should return zero (no-op)
├── Given deadline has expired
│   └── It should revert with ConverterDeadlineExpired
├── Given the supplied adapter is not whitelisted
│   └── It should revert with ConverterAdapterNotAllowed
├── Given the adapter routeTokens view reverts (malformed path)
│   └── It should revert with ConverterAdapterCallFailed
├── Given caller has insufficient tokenIn balance/allowance
│   └── It should revert with ERC20InsufficientBalance / ERC20InsufficientAllowance
├── Given the adapter swap dispatch reverts
│   └── It should revert with ConverterSwapFailed
├── Given the swap output is below _minAmountOut
│   └── It should revert with ConverterInsufficientOutput
└── Given a valid swap
    ├── It should pull tokenIn from the caller
    ├── It should dispatch swap to the caller-supplied adapter via delegatecall (tokens stay on the Converter, single router approval)
    ├── It should transfer the output token to the caller
    ├── It should emit SwapExecuted event
    └── It should return the output amount

Converter::quoteSwapExactAmountIn(address _adapter, bytes _path, uint256 _amountIn)
├── Given the adapter is not whitelisted
│   └── It should revert with ConverterAdapterNotAllowed
├── Given the adapter quote dispatch reverts
│   └── It should revert with ConverterAdapterCallFailed
└── Given the adapter returns a valid quote
    └── It should return the quoted amount

Converter::executeSwapExactAmountOut(address _adapter, bytes _path, uint256 _amountOut, uint256 _amountInMaximum, uint256 _deadline)
├── Given caller does not have caller permission (onlyCaller modifier)
│   └── It should revert with RegistryClientMissingRole(CONVERTER_CALLER_ROLE)
├── Given contract is paused
│   └── It should revert with EnforcedPause
├── Given amountOut is zero
│   └── It should return zero (no-op)
├── Given deadline has expired
│   └── It should revert with ConverterDeadlineExpired
├── Given the supplied adapter is not whitelisted
│   └── It should revert with ConverterAdapterNotAllowed
├── Given the adapter routeTokens view reverts (malformed path)
│   └── It should revert with ConverterAdapterCallFailed
├── Given caller has insufficient tokenIn balance/allowance
│   └── It should revert with ERC20InsufficientBalance / ERC20InsufficientAllowance
├── Given the adapter swap dispatch reverts
│   └── It should revert with ConverterSwapFailed
├── Given the actual input exceeds _amountInMaximum
│   └── It should revert with ConverterExcessiveInput
└── Given a valid exact-output swap
    ├── It should pull up to _amountInMaximum from the caller
    ├── It should dispatch swapExactAmountOut to the adapter via delegatecall (tokens stay on the Converter, single router approval)
    ├── It should refund unused input to the caller
    ├── It should transfer the exact output amount to the caller
    ├── It should emit SwapExecuted event
    └── It should return the actual input spent

Converter::quoteSwapExactAmountOut(address _adapter, bytes _path, uint256 _amountOut)
├── Given the adapter is not whitelisted
│   └── It should revert with ConverterAdapterNotAllowed
├── Given the adapter quoteExactAmountOut dispatch reverts
│   └── It should revert with ConverterAdapterCallFailed
└── Given the adapter returns a valid exact-output quote
    └── It should return the quoted input amount

Converter::setAllowedAdapter(address _adapter, bool _allowed)
├── Given caller does not have ADMIN_ROLE on Registry (onlyAuthRole)
│   └── It should revert with RegistryClientMissingRole
├── Given adapter is zero address
│   └── It should revert with ConverterZeroAddress
├── Given approving a code-less address
│   └── It should revert with ConverterNoCode
├── Given approving a valid adapter
│   ├── It should add the adapter to the allowlist
│   └── It should emit AdapterUpdated(adapter, true)
└── Given removing an adapter
    ├── It should remove the adapter from the allowlist (no code check)
    └── It should emit AdapterUpdated(adapter, false)

Converter::weth()
└── It should return WETH contract address

Converter::isAdapterAllowed(address _adapter)
├── Given adapter is whitelisted
│   └── It should return true
└── Given adapter is not whitelisted
    └── It should return false

Converter::getAllowedAdapters()
└── It should return all whitelisted adapter addresses

Converter::routeTokens(address _adapter, bytes _path)
├── Given the adapter is not whitelisted
│   └── It should revert with ConverterAdapterNotAllowed
├── Given the adapter cannot decode the path
│   └── It should revert with ConverterAdapterCallFailed
└── Given a whitelisted adapter and a valid path
    ├── It should ask the adapter to resolve the route's tokens
    ├── It should return the first token address (input token)
    └── It should return the last token address (output token)

Converter::validateRoute(address _adapter, bytes _route)
├── Given the adapter is not whitelisted
│   └── It should revert with ConverterAdapterNotAllowed
├── Given the adapter validateRoute call reverts
│   └── It should return false (view helper swallows reverts)
├── Given a whitelisted adapter and a valid route
│   └── It should return true
└── Given a whitelisted adapter and an invalid route
    └── It should return false

Converter::isCaller(address _account)
├── Given account has been granted CONVERTER_CALLER_ROLE on the Registry
│   └── It should return true
└── Given account has not been granted CONVERTER_CALLER_ROLE on the Registry
    └── It should return false

Converter::pause()
├── Given caller does not have ADMIN_ROLE on Registry (onlyAuthRole)
│   └── It should revert with RegistryClientMissingRole
├── Given contract is not paused
│   └── It should pause the contract
└── Given contract is already paused
    └── It should revert with EnforcedPause

Converter::unpause()
├── Given caller does not have ADMIN_ROLE on Registry (onlyAuthRole)
│   └── It should revert with RegistryClientMissingRole
├── Given contract is paused
│   └── It should unpause the contract
└── Given contract is not paused
    └── It should revert with ExpectedPause

Converter::_authorizeUpgrade(address _newImplementation)
├── Given caller does not have ADMIN_ROLE on Registry (onlyAuthRole)
│   └── It should revert with RegistryClientMissingRole
└── Given caller has ADMIN_ROLE
    └── It should allow the upgrade

Converter::Access Control Testing
├── Caller permission (onlyCaller)
│   ├── wrapETH / unwrapWETH / executeSwapExactAmountIn / executeSwapExactAmountOut require caller permission (RegistryClientMissingRole)
│   ├── quoteSwapExactAmountIn / quoteSwapExactAmountOut are permissionless (no onlyCaller check)
│   └── grantCallerRole / revokeCallerRole do not require caller permission
├── Registry role gates (onlyAuthRole)
│   ├── setAllowedAdapter requires ADMIN_ROLE on Registry
│   ├── pause / unpause require ADMIN_ROLE on Registry
│   ├── _authorizeUpgrade requires ADMIN_ROLE on Registry
│   └── Non-admin cannot call these functions
├── Registry contract gates (onlyAuthContract)
│   ├── grantCallerRole requires registered StrategyManager contract
│   └── revokeCallerRole requires registered StrategyManager contract
└── Registration
    ├── Converter is registered on the Registry under Auth.CONVERTER key
    └── StrategyManager is registered on the Registry under Auth.STRATEGY_MANAGER key

Converter::Pause Testing
├── Given contract is paused
│   ├── wrapETH / unwrapWETH / executeSwapExactAmountIn / executeSwapExactAmountOut should revert with EnforcedPause
│   ├── setAllowedAdapter should still succeed (no whenNotPaused)
│   ├── quoteSwapExactAmountIn / quoteSwapExactAmountOut should still succeed (no whenNotPaused)
│   ├── view functions should still succeed
│   └── unpause should still succeed
└── Given operations resume after unpause
    └── wrapETH / unwrapWETH / executeSwapExactAmountIn should work again

Converter::Upgrade Testing
├── Given upgrade authorization (caller has ADMIN_ROLE on Registry)
│   ├── It should allow contract upgrades
│   ├── It should maintain state after upgrade (adapters, caller allowlist, weth)
│   └── New functions should work after upgrade
├── Given unauthorized upgrade attempt
│   └── It should revert with RegistryClientMissingRole
└── Given state persistence after upgrade
    ├── Adapter allowlist should remain intact
    ├── Caller permissions should remain intact
    └── WETH should remain set

Converter::Fuzz Testing
├── wrapETH() with random valid amounts
├── unwrapWETH() with random amounts (valid + insufficient balance)
├── executeSwapExactAmountIn() with random valid amounts
├── initialize() with random valid weth address
└── wrapETH() zero amount always no-op

Converter::Registry Integration Testing
├── Generator registered under Auth.CONVERTER key
├── StrategyManager registered under Auth.STRATEGY_MANAGER key
├── Admin has ADMIN_ROLE on Registry
├── Non-admin cannot call setAllowedAdapter
└── Non-StrategyManager cannot call grantCallerRole

UniswapV3ConverterAdapter
├── constructor
│   ├── Given router is zero address
│   │   └── It should revert with UniswapV3ConverterAdapterZeroAddress
│   └── Given quoter is zero address
│       └── It should revert with UniswapV3ConverterAdapterZeroAddress
├── name()
│   └── It should return "UniswapV3ConverterAdapter"
├── validateRoute(bytes)
│   ├── Given a valid single-hop path
│   │   └── It should return true
│   ├── Given a valid multi-hop path
│   │   └── It should return false (single-hop only in initial release)
│   ├── Given a too-short path (< 43 bytes)
│   │   └── It should return false
│   └── Given a misaligned path ((len - 20) % 23 != 0)
│       └── It should return false
├── routeTokens(bytes)
│   ├── Given a valid path
│   │   ├── It should return the first token (input)
│   │   └── It should return the last token (output)
│   └── Given an invalid path
│       └── It should revert with UniswapV3ConverterAdapterInvalidRoute
├── quoteExactAmountIn(bytes, uint256)
│   └── It should return the TWAP-implied output net of the pool fee, Chainlink cross-checked
├── quoteExactAmountOut(bytes, uint256)
│   └── It should return the TWAP-implied input grossed up by the pool fee, Chainlink cross-checked
├── immutables (router / quoter)
│   ├── It should expose the router address set in the constructor
│   └── It should expose the quoter address set in the constructor
└── swapExactAmountIn(bytes, uint256, uint256, address, uint256) [exercised via Converter::executeSwapExactAmountIn]
    └── Given a valid path
        ├── It should pull tokenIn from msg.sender (the Converter)
        ├── It should approve the router and reset the approval after
        ├── It should call router.exactInput with amountOutMinimum == _minAmountOut
        └── It should deliver output to the recipient and return amountOut
├── swapExactAmountOut(bytes, uint256, uint256, address, uint256) [exercised via Converter::executeSwapExactAmountOut]
│   └── Given a valid path
│       ├── It should pull tokenIn from msg.sender (the Converter)
│       ├── It should approve the router with _amountInMaximum and reset the approval after
│       ├── It should reverse the forward-encoded path and call router.exactOutput with amountOut and amountInMaximum
│       ├── It should refund surplus input to msg.sender
│       └── It should deliver output to the recipient and return actual amountIn